From 18926872899cf79527d365c71a80c655ea8776f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vigil Trophies <186610075+guutol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:41:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: record trophy unlocks in user/trophies.jsonl

sceNpTrophyUnlockTrophy now also appends one JSON line per unlock to
<user>/trophies.jsonl, so optional companion tools (achievement trackers)
can read the player's progress. The runtime never touches the network:
it only appends to a local file.

- src/runtime_trophy.c: trophy_store_append() validates the title id
  ([A-Z0-9]{4,16}) and trophy id (0..255), writes each line with a single
  fwrite under a mutex and never aborts.
- probe.c passes the TITLE_ID from param.sfo (fallback CUSA03173).
- trophy_unlock keeps its log line and return values; a failed write is
  only reported on stderr.
- tests/test_trophy.c: standalone test, wired into build.sh --test.
